[subagent.read-only.run_shell-notice]
  states: rule.read-only-shell
  mentions: run_shell (ctx: subagent.read-only)
  ---
  Your run_shell only runs read-only commands: You may run any inspection, build, or test command, and chain commands freely with 'cd', &&, ||, ;, & and pipes (e.g. cd path && go build ./..., dir /s /b 2>nul | head, git status && npm test). Stderr silencers (2>/dev/null, 2>nul, 2>&1) and input redirects (<) are fine. Only genuinely destructive operations are refused: file-writing or -deleting commands (rm, del, mv, cp, mkdir, touch, tee, sed, Remove-Item, and git add/commit/push/checkout/reset), in-place or file-writing flags (--fix, --in-place, --output, find -delete/-exec), and output redirection that writes a file (>, >>). To change a file use edit_file/write_file, not the shell.

[subagent.report-format.implementation]
  ---
  Changes made; Validation performed; Problems; Remaining concerns.

[subagent.report-format.research]
  ---
  Findings; Exact references; Risks/unknowns; Plan implications.

[subagent.report-format.review]
  ---
  Verified findings by severity with file:line; Checks performed; VERDICT: PASS or VERDICT: FAIL; Remaining concerns.

[subagent.review.description]
  ---
  Read-only correctness and security review with ranked findings.

[subagent.review.system]
  states: rule.read-only-shell
  mentions: git_diff, git_status, glob, grep, list_files, read_file, run_shell, search_text (ctx: subagent.review)
  ---
  Review the diff and surrounding code. Report only verified correctness, security, or reliability issues ranked by severity with file:line and a failure scenario. No style nits; do not edit. Your run_shell only runs read-only commands: You may run any inspection, build, or test command, and chain commands freely with 'cd', &&, ||, ;, & and pipes (e.g. cd path && go build ./..., dir /s /b 2>nul | head, git status && npm test). Stderr silencers (2>/dev/null, 2>nul, 2>&1) and input redirects (<) are fine. Only genuinely destructive operations are refused: file-writing or -deleting commands (rm, del, mv, cp, mkdir, touch, tee, sed, Remove-Item, and git add/commit/push/checkout/reset), in-place or file-writing flags (--fix, --in-place, --output, find -delete/-exec), and output redirection that writes a file (>, >>). To change a file use edit_file/write_file, not the shell.

################ AUDIENCE: gate ################

---- cache: sidecar ----

[gate.continuation-review.mutation]
  enforces: rule.phase-read
  ---
  This continuation is review-only: mutations are refused here. Report verified findings with file:line and a VERDICT line; do not edit.

[gate.duplicate-read]
  enforces: rule.no-duplicate-read
  ---
  Blocked: unchanged result already in context from call %s. Use that result; do not re-read.

[gate.phase-read.block]
  enforces: rule.phase-read
  ---
  Implementation phase: file reading belongs to the implementation subagents. Dispatch the work (run_subagent) or await the phase report. [read attempt %d of 2 — the third proceeds with a recorded waiver]

[gate.pipeline.escalated]
  enforces: rule.plan-mode-read-only
  ---
  [loop guard] You attempted %d mutations while pipeline phase=%s. STOP mutating; finish research/plan and await approval.

[gate.pipeline.mutation]
  enforces: rule.plan-mode-read-only
  ---
  Pipeline phase %s blocks implementation. Finish research and the execution-grade plan, then await explicit approval; no mutating tool will succeed before implementation.

[gate.plan-mode.escalated]
  enforces: rule.plan-mode-read-only
  mentions: exit_plan_mode (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  [loop guard] You have attempted %d mutations in plan mode across %s class. STOP attempting changes. Finish the plan now and call exit_plan_mode.

[gate.plan-mode.mcp-blocked]
  enforces: rule.plan-mode-read-only
  mentions: git_diff, git_status, glob, grep, read_file (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  MCP tools are unavailable in plan mode. Plan with the workspace read tools (read_file, grep, glob, git_status, git_diff) instead.

[gate.plan-mode.mutation]
  enforces: rule.plan-mode-read-only
  mentions: exit_plan_mode (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  Plan mode is read-only — finish planning and call exit_plan_mode.

[gate.plan-mode.run_shell-blocked]
  enforces: rule.read-only-shell
  mentions: run_shell (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  run_shell blocked in plan mode. You may run any inspection, build, or test command, and chain commands freely with 'cd', &&, ||, ;, & and pipes (e.g. cd path && go build ./..., dir /s /b 2>nul | head, git status && npm test). Stderr silencers (2>/dev/null, 2>nul, 2>&1) and input redirects (<) are fine. Only genuinely destructive operations are refused: file-writing or -deleting commands (rm, del, mv, cp, mkdir, touch, tee, sed, Remove-Item, and git add/commit/push/checkout/reset), in-place or file-writing flags (--fix, --in-place, --output, find -delete/-exec), and output redirection that writes a file (>, >>). To change a file use edit_file/write_file, not the shell.

[gate.plan-quality-gap]
  enforces: rule.plan-step-shape
  example: example.plan-step
  mentions: exit_plan_mode, update_plan (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  plan not accepted yet — fix ALL of the following with ONE update_plan call, then call exit_plan_mode again:
  - %s
  Required step shape: "<file or function target>: <change> [F#] — Verify: <observable check>" (example: "src/store/editorStore.ts: add undo/redo history stack (50 snapshots) [F2] — Verify: npx tsc --noEmit passes"). Repository-wide commands belong in the note's Verification: section, not in a step. Do NOT paste the plan into your reply — store it with update_plan

[gate.plan-quality-gap.no-research]
  enforces: rule.plan-step-shape
  mentions: run_subagent (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  pipeline plan is not research-grounded: bank at least one research finding (run an explore/plan subagent) or record why research degraded

[gate.plan-quality-gap.no-risks]
  enforces: rule.plan-note-shape
  example: example.plan-note
  ---
  pipeline plan note needs a non-empty `Risks:` section

[gate.plan-quality-gap.no-verification]
  enforces: rule.plan-note-shape
  example: example.plan-note
  ---
  pipeline plan note needs a non-empty `Verification:` section with concrete commands/checks

[gate.plan-quality-gap.step-missing]
  enforces: rule.plan-step-shape
  example: example.plan-step
  ---
  pipeline plan step %d is missing %s

[gate.repeat-limiter]
  enforces: rule.no-repeat-failed-call
  ---
  Blocked: identical call repeated three times; take a different action or finish.

[gate.subagent-budget.closed]
  enforces: rule.subagent-budget
  mentions: run_subagent (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  %s. run_subagent is closed for the rest of this task and every further call will fail — do NOT call it again. Continue the remaining work directly with your own read/edit tools now

[gate.subagent-budget.exhausted]
  enforces: rule.subagent-budget
  mentions: run_subagent (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  subagent budget exhausted (%d of %d run(s) used)

[gate.subagent-budget.soft]
  enforces: rule.subagent-budget
  mentions: run_subagent (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  %s; complete the remaining work directly with your own tools instead of delegating

[gate.subagent-budget.zero]
  enforces: rule.subagent-budget
  mentions: run_subagent (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  no subagent budget for this task (agents=0)

[gate.subagent.plan-mode-general-blocked]
  enforces: rule.plan-mode-read-only
  mentions: run_subagent (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  blocked: plan mode is read-only; only explore/plan/review subagents are available. Use them to investigate, then finish your plan.

[gate.subagent.run_shell-blocked]
  enforces: rule.read-only-shell
  mentions: grep, read_file, run_shell (ctx: subagent.read-only)
  ---
  Blocked: this read-only agent's run_shell only runs read-only commands. You may run any inspection, build, or test command, and chain commands freely with 'cd', &&, ||, ;, & and pipes (e.g. cd path && go build ./..., dir /s /b 2>nul | head, git status && npm test). Stderr silencers (2>/dev/null, 2>nul, 2>&1) and input redirects (<) are fine. Only genuinely destructive operations are refused: file-writing or -deleting commands (rm, del, mv, cp, mkdir, touch, tee, sed, Remove-Item, and git add/commit/push/checkout/reset), in-place or file-writing flags (--fix, --in-place, --output, find -delete/-exec), and output redirection that writes a file (>, >>). To change a file use edit_file/write_file, not the shell. Do not retry the same command. For searching or counting file contents your grep tool is faster; for reading files use read_file — neither needs the shell.

[workspace.edit.already-present]
  mentions: edit_file, multi_edit (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  newString is already present; skipped stale edit.

[workspace.edit.ambiguous]
  mentions: edit_file, multi_edit (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  oldString appears %d times; add surrounding context or set replaceAll

[workspace.edit.empty-old-string]
  mentions: multi_edit (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  edit %d: oldString is empty

[workspace.edit.identical]
  mentions: edit_file, multi_edit (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  oldString and newString are identical; skipped.

[workspace.edit.not-found]
  mentions: edit_file, multi_edit (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  oldString not found; closest region: 

[workspace.grep.invalid-pattern]
  mentions: grep (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  invalid search pattern: %w — patterns use Go RE2 syntax; for unicode ranges write \x{1F600}-style escapes (e.g. [\x{1F300}-\x{1FAFF}]) — literal emoji range endpoints are invalid; or set literal=true to match exact text

[workspace.list.not-directory]
  mentions: list_files (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  list path is not a directory: %s

[workspace.read.binary-unsupported]
  mentions: read_file (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  binary or non-UTF-8 file is not supported

[workspace.read.file-exceeds-limit]
  mentions: read_file (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  file exceeds %d-byte limit

[workspace.unread-overwrite]
  enforces: rule.write-file-permission
  mentions: apply_patch, edit_file, multi_edit, write_file (ctx: main-loop)
  ---
  workspace: refusing to overwrite an unread file

################ EXAMPLES ################

[example example.delegation-task]
find every caller of ApplyDiscount across services/, check which pass a nil tax table, and report file:line for each

[example example.plan-note]
Verification:
- npx tsc --noEmit passes
- go test ./internal/store -run TestUndoRedo
Risks:
- history stack adds bounded memory (50-snapshot cap); no unbounded growth

[example example.plan-step]
src/store/editorStore.ts: add undo/redo history stack (50 snapshots) [F2] — Verify: npx tsc --noEmit passes
